    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. one thing though, if the insurance is the seller's job, what is the specific level of coverage they are required to provide under CIF? i heard there might be different levels depending on the term used.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF Incoterms 2020, the seller is required to procure and pay for maritime insurance covering the goods against loss or damage during transit. The level of coverage is determined by the insurance document issued by the originating country. If a standard policy is issued, which is common, it typically only covers the goods up to their actual cash value, even if that is less than their replacement cost. If a valuable policy is sought, the seller may require the buyer to arrange for a separate insurance policy with adequate coverage. This separate policy should cover the entire loss or damage up to the full replacement value of the goods. The seller, however, is still responsible for providing proof of the insurance policy to the buyer before the goods are handed over at the discharge port.",
